-- title:
--   Monotone families of irreducible closed sets are eventually constant
-- statement:
--   Let $X$ be a locally Noetherian scheme and $x$ a point of $X$. Let $\iota$ be a non-empty preorder and let $Z \colon \iota \to$ `TopologicalSpace.Closeds X` be a family of closed subsets of the underlying topological space of $X$, subject to three hypotheses: each $Z_i$, viewed as a subset of $X$, is irreducible (in particular non-empty); the point $x$ lies in $Z_i$ for every $i$; and $Z$ is monotone, i.e. $Z_i \le Z_{i'}$ whenever $i \le i'$. The conclusion is that there exists an index $i_0 \in \iota$ such that $Z_i = Z_{i_0}$ for every $i$ with $i_0 \le i$, the equality being equality of closed subsets of $X$. Thus an ascending family of irreducible closed subsets all passing through a fixed point of a locally Noetherian scheme stabilises; no cofinality or directedness assumption on $\iota$ is made, and the index $i_0$ is not asserted to be maximal in any sense beyond the stated stabilisation above it.
--
--   This is the ascending chain condition on irreducible closed subsets through a point of a locally Noetherian scheme, a geometric form of the finiteness of heights of primes in a Noetherian local ring. It is used in the construction of the abelian subvariety generated by a family of endomorphisms, where it permits the passage from an arbitrary family to a finite subfamily with the same image, in [`GoodReductionJacobian.RelativeGroupLaw.exists_isClosedImmersion_range_eq_closure_endomorphisms_of_field`](thm.html#GoodReductionJacobian.RelativeGroupLaw.exists_isClosedImmersion_range_eq_closure_endomorphisms_of_field).
